OPERATION ICARUS (Tiny Battle Publishing, 2017)
Designer: Bruce A. Costello
Artist: Ilya Kudriashov
Type: 2-player hex-and-counter wargame
Genre: Hypothetical WWII operational simulation
Theme: German invasion of Iceland (Unternehmen Ikarus / Fall Ikarus)
Historical basis: Cancelled 1940 Kriegsmarine plan using liners Europa & Bremen

SCALE
Turn length: 1 day
Hex size: ~5 km
Unit scale: Company to battalion (land); individual ships / groups (naval); squadrons (air)
Map: Split board — strategic sea areas (North Atlantic / Norway / UK) + tactical hex maps of Iceland (Reykjavik / Akureyri focus)

COMPONENTS
88 unit counters
40 operational markers
1 map
1 two-sided player aid
2 scenario cards (3 scenarios)
1 rulebook

PLAYERS / TIME / COMPLEXITY
Players: 2
Play time: 90–120 min
Complexity: High
Solitaire suitability: Medium
Age: 12+

UNIT TYPES
Land: Infantry, Airborne, Commando, Marine, Artillery, Panzer, Trucks
Naval: Warships, Transports, Submarines / U-boats
Air: Combat, Transport, Reconnaissance
Steps: One-step or two-step (reduced strength on reverse)
Submarines: Hidden (front) / attacking-spotted (back)

KEY VARIABLES / MECHANICS
Transport capacity:
  German Europa: 10 units
  British / US transports: 5 units
Naval movement: 1 sea area per turn (always exposed at sea for at least 1 turn)
Spotting: Required before naval combat
Combined arms: Land + sea + air on same map
Supply / out-of-supply markers
Facility damage: Ports, airbases, bridges
Victory: Control of Reykjavik, Akureyri and key VP hexes
Scenarios: May 1940 / July 1940 / June 1941 (US entry possible)

CORE RISK
German player typically loads the entire invasion force onto a single Europa transport.
If intercepted and sunk before landing, game ends immediately for Germany.
Optional rules exist to split or protect the force.

FUNDAMENTALS
What-if premise: Germany reaches Iceland before or with the British (historical Operation Fork, May 1940).
Objective: Establish air/naval bases to threaten North Atlantic convoys.
German constraint: Weak navy, limited air range, dependence on surprise and one fast liner.
Allied constraint: Recovering from Norway / Dunkirk; must contest landings while protecting sea lanes.
System character: Small physical board, dense interaction rules (land-sea-air linkage).
